From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Circuit-Sword Batocera port <local@circuit-sword>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] remove broken K&R-style forward declarations

xxd.c unconditionally forward-declares strtol()/ftell() with old K&R
no-prototype syntax ("extern long int strtol();"). Modern glibc headers
(stdio.h/stdlib.h, both already included above) declare these with
real prototypes, and GCC treats the mismatch as a hard "conflicting
types" error -- not a warning that can be downgraded via -Wno-error.
The declarations are redundant (the real prototypes are already
visible) and safe to remove.

Not yet submitted upstream -- local fix for this build.

Signed-off-by: Circuit-Sword Batocera port <local@circuit-sword>
---
 xxd.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

--- a/xxd.c
+++ b/xxd.c
@@ -139,8 +139,6 @@
 # endif
 #endif

-extern long int strtol();
-extern long int ftell();

 char version[] = "xxd v1.11, 8 jun 2013 by Juergen Weigert et al.";
 #ifdef WIN32
--
2.39.3
